{% extends 'admin/layout.twig' %}

{#
  What the platform tells its models to do, and which of those instructions somebody here
  has changed.

  The list is driven off the capability registry rather than off the rows, deliberately: a
  screen showing only the prompts somebody already edited is useless for finding the one
  behaving badly, which is the reason anybody opens this page.
#}

{% block head_styles %}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  .ap-lede{ background:#fff; border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.1); border-radius:14px;
    padding:18px 20px; margin-bottom:16px }
  .ap-lede h2{ margin:0 0 8px; font-size:14.5px; color:#10292C }
  .ap-lede p{ margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12.5px; line-height:1.7; color:#5a6d6f; max-width:76ch }
  .ap-lede strong{ color:#10292C }
  .ap-tag{ font-size:10.5px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.05em; text-transform:uppercase;
    padding:3px 8px; border-radius:999px; background:rgba(16,41,44,.07); color:#3d4b4d }
  .ap-tag--on{ background:#eaf7ea; color:#1c5f1b }
  .ap-mut{ font-size:12px; color:#5a6d6f; line-height:1.55 }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block topbar_title %}AI instructions{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

{# ── SAID FIRST, AND PLAINLY ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   The request behind this screen was "let me train the AI". Somebody who believes
   they are training a model will make a real decision on that belief and discover
   it was wrong at the worst moment, so the correction is the first thing here and
   not a footnote under the table. #}
<div class="ap-lede">
  <h2>This changes the instructions, not the model</h2>
  <p><strong>Nothing here trains anything.</strong> Training — or fine-tuning — means a
     training run against a hosted model with a prepared dataset and a bill to match. This
     platform sends requests to other companies' models; there is no way for us to change
     how any of them were built, and anybody who tells you otherwise is selling something.</p>
  <p>What you <em>can</em> change is what we ask them to do: the standing instruction each
     feature sends with every request. That is most of the behaviour you actually notice —
     what it looks for, what it ignores, how it writes. Changing it here takes effect on the
     next request, with no deploy.</p>
  <p><strong>Three things an instruction cannot do</strong>, whatever it says. It cannot let
     a feature approve, reject or rank anybody — that is enforced outside the wording. It
     cannot remove the barrier that stops text somebody submitted from being read as an
     order to the model. And it cannot change the model, the budget or the timeout, which
     live in the code. So the worst a bad edit can do is produce bad answers, which you can
     see in the call log and put back in one press.</p>
</div>

<div class="ad-card">
  <div class="ad-card__head"><div class="ad-card__title">Every AI feature
    <small>the ones you have changed are marked; the rest use the wording that ships with
      the platform</small></div></div>

  <div class="ad-table-wrap">
    <table class="ad-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">AI capabilities and their instructions</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Feature</th>
          <th scope="col">What it is for</th>
          <th scope="col">Model</th>
          <th scope="col">Instruction</th>
          <th scope="col" class="col-actions">&nbsp;</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
      {% for r in rows %}
        <tr>
          <td>
            <strong style="font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace);font-size:12.5px">{{ r.capability }}</strong>
            <div class="ap-mut">
              {% if r.advisory %}Advisory — it can never decide anything.{% endif %}
              {% if r.public %} Reads text the public submitted.{% endif %}
            </div>
          </td>
          <td class="ap-mut">{{ r.purpose }}</td>
          <td class="ap-mut" style="font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace);font-size:11.5px">{{ r.model }}</td>
          <td>
            {% if r.edited %}
              <span class="ap-tag ap-tag--on">Yours · v{{ r.version }}</span>
              {% if r.note %}<div class="ap-mut" style="margin-top:5px">“{{ r.note }}”</div>{% endif %}
              {% if r.changed_at %}<div class="ap-mut">{{ r.changed_at|slice(0,16) }}</div>{% endif %}
            {% else %}
              <span class="ap-tag">As shipped</span>
              {% if r.versions > 0 %}
                <div class="ap-mut" style="margin-top:5px">{{ r.versions }} earlier version(s) kept</div>
              {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          </td>
          <td class="col-actions">
            <a class="ad-btn ad-btn--sm" href="/admin/ai-prompts/{{ r.capability|url_encode }}">
              {{ r.edited ? 'Edit' : 'Change' }}</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
      {% else %}
        <tr><td colspan="5" style="color:var(--ad-text-soft)">No AI features are declared.</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
